UML is a unified modelling language which is a way of visualising and documenting the software by set of diagrams.

Use case diagram
class diagram
activity diagram
sequence diagram


Use Case diagram: It describes functionality of a system. 
Components are: 
  Actors: customer, guest
  system boundary
  include=>calling other function
  extend=> include base+some extended features

Class diagram: How different entities related to each other
Structure:
-----------------
| Class Name    |
-----------------
| Properties    |
-----------------
| Methods       |
-----------------

Relationships:

Association:  A and B call each other (bidirectional A----B)  unidirectional (A-->B) A can call B but not B call A   
Aggregation: A ◇──── B  B can exist without A
Composition: A ◆──── B  B can't exist without A
Multiplicity like *--1   2---1
Generalisation: A implements B (interfaces)
Inheritance: A inherits B


Sequence diagram:
It describes interactions among classes for exchange of messages over time.

Activity diagram:
It represents flow of control in system.
It uses diamonds,start,stop symbols.






